Magicbane will resist most curses for you, if wielded, and
engrave Elbereth in one turn. Wielded, it will provide magic
resistance should you have occasion to remove your GDSM. If
those don't sound important to you, don't get it.

Grayswindr, Frost Brand and Fire Brand seem to be regarded
as the best in class. Grayswindr always doubles damage and
adds silver damage to silver haters. Frost Brand doubles
damage against non cold resistant monsters and adds cold
damage. Fire Brand is the same except substitute fire for
cold. All will allow you to two weapon, usually with a
silver saber or long sword (keep any long sword you get from
an "A" until you can ID it). You could eventually get the
Brands sacrificing since they aren't aligned. Grayswindr
will occasionally blast you (2d4) but cannot be gained by
sacrificing since it is lawful.

Sufficient sacrificing or being crowned will get you
Stormbringer which is a pretty fine weapon itself (level
drains most monsters) and it also allows two weapon combat.
I finished my last game with the +7 Stormbringer two
weaponed with a +3 long sword.

